# Tool Prerequisites

## GitLab CLI (glab)

Required for merge request and code review workflows.

- **Install:** `brew install glab`
- **Authenticate:** `glab auth login`
- **Used by:** `/mr` (create merge requests), `/resolve-reviews` (fetch/reply to MR comments)

If `glab` is not installed or not authenticated, these workflows will not function. Check with `glab --version` and `glab auth status`.

## Atlassian MCP Server (optional)

Required for JIRA integration workflows. Not needed if your team does not use JIRA.

- **Install:** In Claude Code, run `/plugin` and install "Atlassian". In Cursor, add the Atlassian MCP server to `~/.cursor/mcp.json`. In Codex, add to `~/.codex/config.toml`.
- **Authenticate:** In Claude Code, run `/mcp` and select Atlassian. Other tools follow their MCP auth flow.
- **Used by:** `/plan-to-jira` (create JIRA issues from plans), `/update-jira` (update issues with implementation details), auto-transitions in `/execute-plan` and `/finish`

JIRA features are fully optional. All non-JIRA skills work without it. The `/execute-plan` and `/finish` skills silently skip JIRA transitions when no `.jira-map.json` linkage file exists.
